      "role": "user",
      "content": "my bad, forgot u cant pull them directly. here is the diff for the core module:\n\n```diff\n--- a/agent_core/orchestrator.py\n+++ b/agent_core/orchestrator.py\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@\n-from agent_runtime import SessionManager, TaskExecutor\n+from stateless_functions import execute_task\n\n-class AgentOrchestrator:\n+class LegacyOrchestrator:\n     def __init__(self):\n-        self.session = SessionManager()\n+        self.session = None # Deprecated: moving to stateless execution\n```\n\nit basically swaps out the `agent_runtime` (the part that handles your persistent context and loop) for those simple stateless functions the team wants to use instead. let me know if the `LegacyOrchestrator` class structure looks okay for the transition period or if it'll break anything in the current build.",
